      {
        "id": 70106,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-07T01:55:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarkJ\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/a183cd/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarkJ:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My main question which was raised with Jemsk during play last weekend is does a card drawn as a result as an End of Turn count as being as in play at the end of the turn, or does it not count as played until after the turn? &nbsp;We played the latter.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Cards are played during the end-of-turn, and they would trigger end-of-turn effects if they have them.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MarkJ\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/a183cd/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MarkJ:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And unless we're missing something there's no such thing as End of Turn card priority - that it's up to the players to determine the order in which End of Turn effects are carried out.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The players cannot choose the order. All cards are carried out in the order that they entered play. So if there are multiple cards out with end-of-turn effects, they will go into effect in the order that they were played.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:48:52.010Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 8488,
        "topic_slug": "end-of-turn-effects-for-cards-drawn-at-end-of-turn",
        "display_username": "Pydro",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"MarkJ\"]\n\n My main question which was raised with Jemsk during play last weekend is does a card drawn as a result as an End of Turn count as being as in play at the end of the turn, or does it not count as played until after the turn? &nbsp;We played the latter. \n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n Cards are played during the end-of-turn, and they would trigger end-of-turn effects if they have them. \n\n \n[quote=\"MarkJ\"]\n \n\n And unless we&#39;re missing something there&#39;s no such thing as End of Turn card priority - that it&#39;s up to the players to determine the order in which End of Turn effects are carried out. \n\n \n[/quote]\n \n\n The players cannot choose the order. All cards are carried out in the order that they entered play. So if there are multiple cards out with end-of-turn effects, they will go into effect in the order that they were played. \n",
