        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-07T15:04:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The bit that causes confusion is that if things appear to happen simultaneously, they don't, and you can choose the order they happen in. Example: a single card hits all targets for damage, you choose the order the damage is applied in. But <em>cards themselves</em> are still resolved in the order they were played.</p>",
